## Example reverse proxy for a plain VPS deployment.
## Caddy auto-provisions and renews a Let's Encrypt TLS certificate for the domain below —
## this is what makes the API reachable over HTTPS (required once the frontend is HTTPS).
## Not needed on platforms that already terminate TLS for you (Fly.io, Render, Railway).
##
## Usage: point api.yourdomain.com's DNS A/AAAA record at this server, then:
##   caddy run --config Caddyfile.example

api.yourdomain.com {
    reverse_proxy localhost:8787
}
